{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And you shall bring the bull before the tent of meeting.</b> Ibn Ezra said (on Exodus 29:10) that its meaning is: when you bring the bull before the tent of meeting, Aaron and his sons shall lay their hands upon it, for he had already mentioned this above (Exodus 29:3). But the correct interpretation in my eyes is as I explained (there): there He commands to bring them, but did not specify before the tent of meeting — only that he shall bring them. The reason he brings them to the place of the priests is that they be ready, and it suffices that they be before the entrance of the court of the Mishkan. But now He requires that he bring them before the tent of meeting, to the entrance of the tent, as He will explain in the section on slaughter (Exodus 29:11), for the semikhah (laying on of hands) is to take place there."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:18:00.341390878Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}